\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|c1-a4-mathlib~}}\td{the same}\td{ten Mathlib slices (\code{\verb~|Scheme~}, \code{\verb~|Sylow~}, \code{\verb~|Order.Basic~}, \code{\verb~|Fintype.Basic~}, \code{\verb~|Topology.Basic~}, \code{\verb~|Group.Basic~}, \code{\verb~|Nat.Basic~}, \code{\verb~|List.Basic~}, \code{\verb~|Galois.Basic~}, \code{\verb~|Pow.Real~})}\td{108,256}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0 / 0 / 0}\td{10 of 10 right}\td{PASS WITH DECLINES}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|c1-d4~}}\td{D + \code{\verb~|m4b~} (D = the published default set of 19:41Z), session cap 1 MiB}\td{the seven corpora as above}\td{the same}\td{0}\td{0}\td{tier 0, audits 0; \strong{convention: Std 1,725 (D0) / 1,604 (unbounded), Cedar slice 12 / 12 declarations differ} - see below}\td{230 of 230 and the four corpora right; MACHINE-INCOMPLETE 0}\td{FAIL (convention part)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|c1-d4-again~}}\td{the same, the complete gate a second time}\td{the seven corpora}\td{the same}\td{0}\td{0}\td{tier 0, audits 0; \strong{convention: Std 1,199 / 2,780, Cedar slice 0 / 15}}\td{right}\td{FAIL (convention part)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|c1-d4-conv~}}\td{the same}\td{Std, reachability, the Cedar slice; convention part only}\td{112,384}\td{0}\td{0}\td{convention 0}\td{-}\td{PASS WITH DECLINES}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|report.sh conv~} on Std (D128, D64, D0, unbounded)}\td{D + \code{\verb~|m4b~}; D}\td{Std}\td{100,096 each}\td{-}\td{-}\td{EQUIVALENT, both}\td{-}\td{-}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|c1-d-control~}}\td{\strong{D WITHOUT \code{\verb~|m4b~}} (the published default set on the same copy)}\td{the seven corpora}\td{the same}\td{0}\td{0}\td{tier 0, audits 0; \strong{convention: Cedar slice 73 declarations differ (D0)}}\td{right}\td{FAIL (convention part)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|c1-d4-mathlib~}}\td{D + \code{\verb~|m4b~}}\td{four Mathlib slices (\code{\verb~|Scheme~}, \code{\verb~|Sylow~}, \code{\verb~|Order.Basic~}, \code{\verb~|Galois.Basic~}); differential + audits}\td{68,969}\td{0}\td{0}\td{audits 0}\td{-}\td{PASS WITH DECLINES}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|c1-rich4~}}\td{rich + \code{\verb~|m4b~} (with \code{\verb~|k2~}, \code{\verb~|probes~}, \code{\verb~|facts~}), cap 4 MiB}\td{the seven corpora}\td{the same}\td{0}\td{0}\td{tier 0, audits 0; \strong{convention: Std 12,073 / 1,037, reachability 44, Cedar slice 43}}\td{right}\td{FAIL (convention part)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|c1-rich-control~}}\td{rich WITHOUT \code{\verb~|m4b~}}\td{Std, reachability, the Cedar slice; convention part only}\td{112,384}\td{0}\td{0}\td{convention 0}\td{-}\td{PASS WITH DECLINES}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|c1-rich4-mathlib~}}\td{rich + \code{\verb~|m4b~}}\td{three Mathlib slices; differential + audits}\td{42,427}\td{0}\td{0}\td{audits 0}\td{-}\td{PASS WITH DECLINES}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|report.sh conv~} (D128, D64, D0, unbounded)}\td{20 switch sets: \code{\verb~|m4b~} with each switch of D alone, D + \code{\verb~|m4b~} complete, D + \code{\verb~|m4b~} minus one switch at a time}\td{the Cedar slice}\td{8,064 each}\td{-}\td{-}\td{EQUIVALENT in all 20 (\code{\verb~|work/c1/logs/bisect.done~})}\td{-}\td{-}}
}

\p{\strong{The convention differences of the complete gate are not reproducible outside it and exist without the patch} (finding C1-F2, for M8 / M7 / the integrator). (1) The complete gate of the published default set WITHOUT \code{\verb~|m4b~}, on the same copy and harness, shows them (\code{\verb~|c1-d-control~}: 73 declarations of the Cedar slice, "the same number of call events, distributed differently over the ops"). (2) With \code{\verb~|m4b~}, the convention part run alone on the three corpora is clean (\code{\verb~|c1-d4-conv~}), and so is the dedicated report \code{\verb~|report.sh conv~}: on Std with D + \code{\verb~|m4b~} and with D (100,096 declarations, four depth bounds, EQUIVALENT), on the Cedar slice with D + \code{\verb~|m4b~} and 19 subsets. (3) Which declarations differ changes from run to run (Cedar slice: 12 / 12, then 0 / 15 with the patch, 73 / 0 without), they lie late in the file, and in every run the outcomes, the tier comparison, the audits and the pipeline are clean. So something that the parts of one gate JVM share (the code and fact store, the \code{\verb~|pchk~} bits, or the heap: a growth that \code{\verb~|heapAllows~} refuses gives a lane a fresh session) moves ticks between lanes when all parts run at once; the integrator's own gate of the default set did not show it (requests.log 19:41Z). I did not find which one. What I cannot exclude: the differences on Std appeared in both complete runs with the patch (from unit 82,426 on) and not in the one complete run without it. For the patch this means: its convention equivalence is established where the comparison is reproducible (\code{\verb~|c1-a4~} with all parts, \code{\verb~|c1-a4-mathlib~}, \code{\verb~|c1-d4-conv~}, the 22 \code{\verb~|conv~} reports), and whether the complete gate of D + \code{\verb~|m4b~} is less stable than that of D is open.}

\p{The declines are those of the base tree: the eager-reduction rule (M6-F26: 164 units of Init, 203 of Std, 8 of reachability, 11 of the Cedar slice, 28 of the \code{\verb~|Scheme~} slice, ...) and, in the step-1 set under the harness heap of 5 GiB, three \code{\verb~|perf~} tests by \code{\verb~|E_MEM~} (\code{\verb~|loop-unfolded-once~}, \code{\verb~|magma-list-deep-n36~}, \code{\verb~|magma-list-pair-n21~}; they are accepted with \code{\verb~|same~}).}
}

\subtree{
\title{7.2 Hostile exports}

\p{\code{\verb~|work/c1/judge.py~}: every export through the launcher classes of the clean private tree with \code{\verb~|-X engine=machine~}; official verdicts from the owners' records (package S's manifest, S2's judged tables) and, for the new exports, from leanchecker 4.36.0 run in the arena container (\code{\verb~|work/c1/official.sh~}). Switch sets: \code{\verb~|a4~} = \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect,m4b~}; \code{\verb~|f4~} = \code{\verb~|a4~} + \code{\verb~|facts,probes~}; \code{\verb~|rich4~} = \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect,facts,probes,tele,code,casetrees,lazyeval,same,m2a,m3a,m7a,k2,m4b~}; \code{\verb~|all4~} = \code{\verb~|all,lazyeval,same,match,joint,k2,m2a,m3a,m7a,m4b~} with \code{\verb~|elabAt=1~}; \code{\verb~|only4~} = \code{\verb~|m4b~} alone; \code{\verb~|cap4~} = session cap 1 KiB; \code{\verb~|d0~} = host depth 0.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Set}\th{Exports (official reject / accept)}\th{Switch sets}\th{WRONG verdicts}\th{Declined by the pipeline}}
\tr{\td{package S, the rows of its manifest}\td{327 (282 / 45)}\td{\code{\verb~|a4~}, \code{\verb~|f4~}, \code{\verb~|rich4~}, \code{\verb~|all4~}}\td{0}\td{1 (\code{\verb~|str-lit-missing-prerequisites-bad~}, by design)}}
\tr{\td{S2's table of known exports: all of package S (351) and the arena's \code{\verb~|bad~} tests (92)}\td{443 (396 / 47)}\td{\code{\verb~|dflt4~} (the published default set of 19:41Z + \code{\verb~|m4b~}), \code{\verb~|dflt4j4~} (the same with four workers)}\td{0}\td{1 (the same)}}
